ominated Grid:** **Consequential LCA (CLCA)** is *critical*.  Here, the consequences are potentially severe. CLCA must model the increased fossil fuel consumption resulting from hydrogen production, alongside any potential displacement of other fossil-based technologies. Data collection needs to focus on the marginal electricity mix, potential for lock-in to fossil infrastructure, and impacts on carbon pricing/regulation. Stakeholders (environmental groups, regulators) will demand a thorough understanding of the net climate impact. (Weidema, 2003).\n\n\n\n**Justification:** The energy company’s question explicitly asks about *impacts compared to a baseline*. This necessitates CLCA, which explicitly models system changes. While ALCA provides a useful baseline for comparison, it cannot capture the dynamic consequences of adopting hydrogen production at scale.\n\n\n\n**References:**\n\nBrentrup, F., et al. (2017). *Life Cycle Assessment (LCA) of Biofuels*. Springer.\nEcoinvent. (2023). *Principles of LCA*. [https://ecoinvent.org/database/principles-of-lca/](https://ecoinvent.org/database/principles-of-lca/)\nWeidema, B. P. (2003). LCA in a changing world: challenges and opportunities. *Journal of Industrial Ecology*, *7*(1), 1–11.\n\n\n\n', role='assistant', tool_calls=None, function_call=None, provider_specific_fields=None))], usage=Usage(completion_tokens=643, prompt_tokens=215, total_tokens=858, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None))
